sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Client as CLI client
    participant AS as AS (inside KDC process)
    participant TGS as TGS (inside same KDC process)
    participant RS as Separate resource server

    Note over Client,RS: Draft flow; the custom JSON message format is an educational simulator, not Kerberos wire protocol.
    Client->>AS: POST /login (synthetic username and password)
    AS->>AS: Verify password; create TGT for audience tgs and Kc,tgs
    AS-->>Client: TGT + Kc,tgs delivered separately (local simulator)

    Client->>TGS: POST /service-ticket (TGT + authenticator MACed with Kc,tgs)
    Note right of Client: Authenticator binds request context and a fresh request_nonce.
    TGS->>TGS: Validate TGT audience tgs, time, identity, MAC; consume TGS request
    TGS->>TGS: Create service ticket for audience files and Kc,files
    TGS-->>Client: Service ticket + Kc,files delivered separately (local simulator)

    loop Each resource request
        Client->>Client: Create fresh request_nonce; MAC authenticator with Kc,files
        Client->>RS: POST /access-resource (service ticket + body + authenticator)
        Note right of RS: The service ticket is for audience files; RS never accepts a TGT.
        RS->>RS: Validate service ticket, request context, timestamp, nonce and MAC
        RS->>RS: Apply selected replay-cache mode; execute increment on acceptance
        RS-->>Client: Grant or stable error (e.g. 409 replay_detected)
    end
